  "body": "Create something truly special for modern living. This substantial 1950's concrete and brick home has seen updates over the years, but there is clear scope to renovate or develop this flat freehold 809sqm (more or less) site. With four bedrooms, two bathrooms, a study and three separate living areas, there is already an impressive amount of space to work with, complemented by a large double garage and dedicated workshop. \r\n\r\nFor families, the full site offers plenty of room to enjoy now while opening the door to future possibilities. Refresh the existing home, reshape the living spaces to suit your lifestyle, or explore the potential to add a pool and create a private outdoor haven, subject to the necessary approvals. Zoned Residential Mixed Housing Suburban, the property may also appeal to developers and land bankers looking to unlock further value from a generous Glendowie landholding.\r\n\r\nThe location adds even more appeal, with Glendowie Park approximately 200 metres away and excellent schooling close at hand. Zoned for Glendowie School and Glendowie College, this is a well-positioned address for families wanting to establish themselves in the area. St Heliers Beach and village are approximately 2.3km away or around a five-minute drive, providing easy access to the waterfront, cafes, shops and everyday amenities. With land, space and genuine potential, this is a property ready for its next chapter. Don't miss out on this exciting opportunity.",
